\textbf{Solution:} \text{Given that, we know } C(0, -3) \\
\text{Substituting points } \[A(-3, 0), B(1, 0), \text{ and } C(0, -3) \text{ into the parabola equation } y=ax^{2}+bx+c \text{ yields}\] \\
\[
\begin{cases}
9a+3b+c=0 \\
a+b+c=0 \\
c=-3
\end{cases}
\text{Solving this, we get: }
\begin{cases}
a=1 \\
b=2 \\
c=-3
\end{cases}
\]
\text{Therefore, the quadratic function is given by } \boxed{y=x^{2}+2x-3}

