Reasoning: The problem gives A(-3,0), B(1,0). A is rotated counterclockwise around the origin to point C on the negative half-axis of the y-axis. Rotation keeps the distance to the origin unchanged, so OA=3, therefore the coordinates of C are (0,-3). Let the parabola be y=ax^2+bx+c, substitute A(-3,0), B(1,0), C(0,-3):
Point A: 9a-3b+c=0;
Point B: a+b+c=0;
